      "message": "the delay is definitely TCPC chip specific, and unlikely to be board specific.\n\nthe delay exists in board_reset_pd_mcu(void), but we only want to\nreset a specific pd_mcu (TCPC).  this is the wrapper around\nset_tcpc_power_mode(port) that takes care of the delay.\n\ni\u0027m not too confident about adding the delay to board_set_tcpc_power_mode() because it\u0027ll slow down all\nof its callers.  maybe that\u0027s OK, and maybe that\u0027s the\ncorrect thing to do to meet timing requirements.\n\npd_restart_tcpc() is such a rare and slow code path in any\ncase where i didn\u0027t think about it very much.",
